<title>TANZANIA: Tanzania sells tobacco and cable assets.</title>
<headline>Tanzania sells tobacco and cable assets.</headline>
<byline>Mark Dodd</byline>
<dateline>DAR ES SALAAM 1997-07-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tanzania's Parastatal Sector Reform Commission (PSRC), responsible for divesting government assets, concluded deals totalling $27.6 million for assets in state-owned tobacco and cable manufacturing companies last week, senior officials said on Sunday.</p>
<p>A major U.S company, Universal Leaf Tobacco of Virginia, bought assets worth $16.3 million from the state-run Tanzania Tobacco Board (TTB), PSRC officials told Reuters.</p>
